        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Meet and identify people",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Put the subject before 是 and the identity after it. 不 before 是 negates the identity; 吗 at the end asks a yes-or-no question. In a clear identification context a reply may be short, as in 是我 or 不是我.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "他是好人。",
                "pinyin": "tā shì hǎorén 。",
                "meaning": "He is a good person.",
                "audio": "e21ee309921b5af78d108592e9433db5d6162ea2caada9242f25e42af2ec3e0f"
              },
              {
                "text": "是我。",
                "pinyin": "shì wǒ 。",
                "meaning": "It is me.",
                "audio": "aded91a90b39365dd2994fc812d5109687b01beff0bb91c5628992634ffc9b2c"
              },
              {
                "text": "不是我。",
                "pinyin": "bù shì wǒ 。",
                "meaning": "It is not me.",
